# TwinCAT object files must round-trip byte-exact: they carry a UTF-8 BOM, object GUIDs,
# and whichever line endings the authoring tool left behind. XAE writes CRLF; most published
# code is LF (2839 files measured: 97% BOM, 19% CRLF). Normalising either way rewrites whole
# files and ruins diffs, so -text disables all conversion regardless of core.autocrlf.
*.TcPOU  -text
*.TcDUT  -text
*.TcGVL  -text
*.TcIO   -text
*.TcTTO  -text
*.TcVIS  -text
# Project containers carry the same BOM and line endings, and evals/fixture-project
# depends on its .plcproj arriving byte-for-byte.
*.plcproj -text
*.tsproj  -text
